(*
expect:
same true
cross ticks 10
done
*)
(* rete#244 INVERTED this file (2026-08-25). Its previous life pinned the
   footgun that cost a night (tuvm#94): `platform timers` answered a FRESH
   Timers per call, each with its own `pending` registry and its own colliding
   token counter, so a timer registered through one fetch and dispatched
   through another was armed in C, fired correctly — and was dropped silently.
   A MagTag clock ran 9h23m overnight and struck ZERO of ~19 bells that way.
   The old text here ended: "If a future change makes a foreign registration
   deliverable, this test is the one that must be revisited." This is that
   revisit.

   The accessor now answers THE per-kernel singleton, so the two fetches ARE
   one instance and the cross-fetch registration delivers. Both halves are
   pinned: identity (`same true` — two sends of the accessor answer one
   object) and behaviour (a repeater armed via fetch `b`, dispatched via fetch
   `a`, delivers every fire). The clock is stepped in ten explicit 30 ms
   advances rather than one 300 ms leap, so the expected count does not
   depend on how a large advance coalesces a repeater.

   Explicit construction (`Timers usingSpace:seam:`) still mints fresh
   instances for tests that need a private registry — the class-side door is
   unchanged; only the accessor stopped lying about being one. *)
class TimersInstanceIdentity packageUsing: manifest = ( | private ticks ::= 0. | ) (
  public main: platform args: args = (
    | space a b ping |
    space:: platform space.
    a:: platform timers.
    b:: platform timers.
    ('same ' , (a == b) printString) out.

    (* dispatch through fetch `a`, register through fetch `b` — the exact
       shape that used to drop every event. *)
    space whenever: 'sys/timer' do: [ :e | a dispatch: e ].
    ping:: space channel: 'ping'.
    ping whenever: '' do: [ :m | ticks:: ticks + 1 ].
    b every: 30 post: #o on: ping.

    1 to: 10 do: [ :i |
      platform advanceMillis: 30. space drain ].
    ('cross ticks ' , ticks printString) out.
    'done' out.
  )
) : (
)
